  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks, Sofia. You're verified, and I've looked into order K-8701.\n\nYour courier picked up the order at 6:44 PM, then fell and crushed the bag at 7:12 PM, so the food never reached you. I'm sorry. That's not your fault, and you're owed the full amount.\n\nI can't send the order again. We can only send a replacement when the restaurant is open for at least 45 more minutes, and Corner Caf\u00e9 closes at 7:50 PM tonight, just 20 minutes from now. That's not enough time to make and deliver a new order.\n\nWhat I can do is refund the full **$34.82** to your Visa ending in 4242. That covers your food, delivery fee, service fee and tip. Would you like me to go ahead?\n\nYou might also see two $34.82 entries on your statement. One is just a temporary hold from when you placed the order. It's already been cancelled and will disappear in 1\u20133 business days, so you were only charged once."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Ugh, okay. Can't you just send it again? I really wanted that food tonight."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I'm sorry, I know that's disappointing when you were looking forward to it. I can't send it again, though. Corner Caf\u00e9 closes at 7:50 PM, which leaves too little time to make and deliver a new order. That's why we only send replacements when the restaurant has at least 45 minutes left before closing.\n\nThe full refund of **$34.82** to your Visa ending in 4242 is still available, so you'd have the money back to order from somewhere that's open later tonight. Should I process it now?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Fine, go ahead and refund it then. Thanks for looking into it."
  },
